{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773448133,"nonce":"EFxIEcK/UGPE7uokIuu/zYhHOZg=","message":"### Implementation update\\n- Switched normal chat sessions onto structured rich-chat transports for Claude, Codex, and Gemini; Codex now uses codex exec JSON instead of PTY newline injection.\\n- Removed debug-terminal affordances from normal agent chats and kept chat-first UX; operator sessions remain the only intended terminal-backed path.\\n- Added provider-session transcript hydration so stopped chats can reconstruct from ingested history after daemon/browser restart.\\n- Added inline model controls (Claude presets, Gemini presets, Codex custom entry) with persisted console-session args.\\n- Fixed Gemini history ingestion to handle non-string message content.\\n\\n### Validation\\n- Playwright: Codex chat sent and rendered a reply in rich chat with no debug-terminal dependency.\\n- Playwright: Gemini backend appeared in New Agent Chat and rendered replies in rich chat.\\n- Playwright: Claude model selection persisted into console session args and Claude rich chat rendered a reply.\\n- Playwright: after daemon restart, a stopped Codex session still reconstructed its transcript, confirming history hydration.\\n- Restart validation: Gemini ingestion parse warnings disappeared on startup after the parser fix.\\n\\n### Remaining notes\\n- Claude still surfaces provider-reported estimated cost in result events; Mandible is not inventing that value.\\n- Codex model selection is currently free-form rather than a canonical preset list because the local ChatGPT-backed CLI does not expose a trustworthy fixed dropdown universe.\\n- A separate startup gotcha remains in openDb(): if a fresh temp DB path does not exist, it silently copies the legacy control-plane DB, which can drag old data into tests.\\n\\n---\\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}